2-18T15:48:35Z","closed_at":"2019-04-10T01:11:28Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Seems a regression in SQLAlchemy 1.3.2. With SQLAlchemy up to 1.3.1 I can use a pg service file to declare db endpoints as described in https://www.postgresql.org/docs/11/libpq-pgservice.html\r\n\r\nWith the following snipet of code:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# tst.py\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine, inspector\r\nengine = create_engine(\"postgresql:///?service=swh-log\")\r\ninspector = inspect(engine)\r\nprint(inspector.get_table_names())\r\n```\r\n\r\nI have:\r\n```bash\r\n(swh) $ pip install 'SQLAlchemy<1.3.2'\r\nRequirement already satisfied: SQLAlchemy<1.3.2 in /home/ddouard/.virtualenvs/swh/lib/python3.5/site-packages (1.3.1)\r\n(swh) $ python tst.py\r\n['log', 'dbversion']\r\n(swh) $ strace -e open python tst.py 2>&1  | grep service\r\nopen(\"/home/ddouard/.pg_service.conf\", O_RDONLY) = 3\r\n(swh) $\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut with 1.3.2:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n(swh) $ pip install 'SQLAlchemy==1.3.2'\r\nCollecting SQLAlchemy==1.3.2\r\nInstalling collected packages: SQLAlchemy\r\n  Found existing installation: SQLAlchemy 1.3.1\r\n    Uninstalling SQLAlchemy-1.3.1:\r\n      Successfully uninstalled SQLAlchemy-1.3.1\r\nSuccessfully installed SQLAlchemy-1.3.2\r\n(swh) $ python tst.py \r\n[]\r\n(swh) $ strace -e open python tst.py 2>&1  | grep service\r\n(swh) $\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo in this later case, we see that:\r\n1. the .pg_service.conf is not even loaded,\r\n2. the failed connection to the db is not reported (with <1.3.2 I get a traceback if I try to use a invalid connection url `postgresql:///?service=nowhere`)\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":""